          "english_quote": "and this multitude is diverse, each bird differing from another in every respect",
          "issue": "The distributive interpretation is defensible, but “each bird” makes a referent choice that the note treats as settled. The masculine singular οὗτος and ἐξηλλαγμένος grammatically refer to ὄχλος; τὸν ἕτερον can therefore be understood as another multitude or group, rather than necessarily another individual bird. This affects whether the stated differences concern individuals or groups/kinds.",
